meta {
  name: conditions
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/standards/versions/{{standardVersionId}}/conditions
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Every applicability condition on one standard version, with what the model guessed, what a person
  decided, and which governs.

  `requirementSetVersion` null means the version has no published set — meaningfully different from
  a set with no conditions, and the two used to be indistinguishable here.

  In production this returns an EMPTY list: REQSET-V1 predates the field that stores conditions, so
  there is nothing to review. That is the feature working, not failing.

  Per row: extractedRole vs effectiveRole is the measurement. The extractor over-predicts
  SCOPE_GATE heavily — 117 proposed, 0 confirmed in one reviewed corpus — and `reclassified` flags
  the rows where review disagreed. `canDriveNotApplicable` is separate from the role: a confirmed
  scope gate that nobody authorised still cannot exclude.
}
